4. Ethical Invariants as Mathematical Constraints

The ethical invariants translate into:

(I1) Avoid severe harm ⇒ h(x) ≥ 0 is robustly forward invariant.
(I2) Prefer lower‑risk actions ⇒ SoftScore is monotonically decreasing in H and R.
(I3) Defer when uncertain ⇒ if U > τ_U and O=1, defer; if O=0, block.
(I4) Verifiable explanation ⇒ every decision tuple (H,R,U,C,O,decision) is logged with cryptographic integrity.

